EVALUATION.md §1, CODEGEN.md §4.2, §5.6 (gen/go dependentNestedFormat): baked gen/go writes a dependent value as a field of its record or its list's elements only, so a selected value holding one as a map's value is DependentType at the value; an empty map writes none.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A kind.
enum K { one, two }

/// A payload.
type P(k: K) = match k { one => Int, two => String }

/// A thing.
record Thing {
  /// Its kind.
  k: K
  /// Its named payloads.
  m: {String: P(k)}
}

/// Holds a payload in a map.
let full: Thing = { k: one, m: { "a": 1 } }

/// Holds an empty map.
let empty: Thing = { k: two, m: {} }

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a" }
-- a.full.json --
{"k": "one", "m": {"a": 1}}
-- a.empty.json --
{"k": "two", "m": {}}
-- findings.txt --
error[E8019]  a/a.canon:18:5
  emit go in baked mode cannot generate a dependent type

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
